// Every declaration production begins `annotations, ...`, so the physical-nesting
// guard has to look past them. `@co.dap.local` is the specific annotation worth
// covering: it is what the diagnostic recommends, so a reader who half-remembers
// the rule writes it here — in the nested position — rather than on a declaration
// in its own file. Testing at the raw cursor saw the "@" and declined, sending
// exactly that reader to an unrelated field-grammar error.
_ co.lang.class = {

    @co.dap.local
    Address co.lang.struct = {
        city co.lang.string;
    }
}
